@startuml OpenFinder_Plugin_Execution
title OpenFinder Plugin Discovery and Execution
skinparam shadowing false

actor User
participant "AppModel" as App
participant "PluginManagementService" as Management
participant "PluginRegistry" as Registry
participant "TaskQueueService" as Queue
participant "PluginExecuteTaskHandler" as Handler
participant "PluginExecutionCoordinator" as Coordinator
participant "PluginRunnerRouter" as Router
participant "ProcessPluginRunner" as Process
participant "HTTPPluginRunner" as HTTP
participant "ArtifactResultService" as Artifacts
participant "Result Handler Registry" as Results
participant "Renderer Catalog" as Renderer

App -> Management: scan(built-in, user, development)
Management -> Registry: scanWithDiagnostics(each directory)
Registry --> Management: loaded plugins + diagnostics
Management --> App: priority-resolved catalog
App -> App: match actions against selection

User -> App: invoke plugin action
App -> Queue: enqueue immutable descriptor
Queue -> Handler: execute payload version 1
Handler -> Coordinator: run exact plugin/version/action
Coordinator -> Router: run PluginInput

alt process manifest schema 1
  Router -> Process: stdin JSON + credential environment
  Process --> Coordinator: NDJSON events + exit code
else HTTP manifest schema 2
  Router -> HTTP: loopback job protocol v1
  HTTP --> Coordinator: validated SSE/poll events
end

Coordinator -> Coordinator: validate single final terminal result
Coordinator -> Artifacts: commit confined file artifacts
Artifacts --> Coordinator: committed result context
Coordinator -> Results: handle by output.resultType
Results --> App: typed or generic projection
App -> Renderer: lookup by schema + projection type
Renderer --> App: structured or generic renderer
App --> User: present durable result

note over Handler,Coordinator
Descriptors contain credential references,
never plaintext secret values.
end note

note over Results,Renderer
Plugin ID does not participate
in result or renderer selection.
end note
@enduml
